{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he shall slaughter it</b> etc. It in the north; but the bird, the shelamim, the firstborn, the tithe, and the pesaḥ are not in the north." "<b>On the side of the altar.</b> Beside the side of the altar — like ״וסכות על הארון״." "<b>The side of the altar northward.</b> So that the side of the altar is in the north. And where are its faces? In the south — we learn that the ramp is in the south." "<b>Northward before YHWH.</b> So that the entire north is entirely open. Also the cattle-stone mentioned above stands there, since its slaughter is in the north — for it too is written of it לפני ה׳. And if one slaughtered it in the south of the altar, that is not לפני ה׳, because most of the altar and its ramp stand in the south, and it does not appear facing the entrance of the Hall. But when one slaughters it in the north, which is entirely open and is not a place where the priests tread — since the ramp is in the south — there it is opposite the Hall, and that is לפני ה׳. And He fixed a place for slaughter for kodshei kodashim, as it is written: ״במקום אשר תשחט את העולה תשחט את החטאת,״ and it is written: ״כי כחטאת האשם״ — since their slaughter is fundamentally toward Heaven. But for kodshim kalim no fixed place was set for their slaughter, since they are not so fundamentally toward Heaven."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:52.351364443Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}